questions.stem_md:
For the equation $x^2 + 2(k + 2)x + 9k = 0$:

(a) find the values of $k$ for which the roots are equal;

(b) find the equal root for each of these values of $k$;

(c) show that the equation has no real roots when $k = 2$, and solve it when $k = 6$, giving the roots correct to two decimal places.
